<title>USA: Exxon mulling Baton Rouge plant re storm.</title>
<headline>Exxon mulling Baton Rouge plant re storm.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp said it will issue a status report shortly on its 432,000 barrels per day refinery in Baton Rouge, Louisiana, near the path hurricane Danny is taking.</p>
<p>The spokesman would not say whether Exxon had decided to shut the plant as a precautionary measure.</p>
<p>Shutting a refinery can take a day or two and a decision must be taken in before the worst part of the storm is upon the plant.</p>
<p>Earlier Friday, Chevron Corp said it would close its refinery in Mississippi as the storm looked set to pass near the plant.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
